// Rung 11-d's emission scene: the openvdb.org explosion, whose temperature
// field rides beside its density on the same lattice — the pyro contract
// every solver writes. The field is normalized to [0, 0.885], so the scale
// below is what states its Kelvin: a 3100 K core falling away to nothing at
// the edges, which is where a fire's color comes from.
//
// Emission is collected at the tracker's collisions and never sampled
// toward, so there is no light in frame and no next-event estimation: the
// fire lights only itself, through the smoke it is made of. A dim sky keeps
// the cold shoulders of the plume readable.
//
// The emission scale is large because it carries two small physical
// numbers at once. A blackbody's visible radiance is normalized against
// 6500 K, and this fire tops out near 4700 K; and emission rides on
// absorption, which smoke this thin sets at a hundredth. Scene load prints
// where the pair lands — "a thick core settles at 12.8" — so the 400 is
// arithmetic rather than a knob turned until it looked right. The offset
// matters for the same reason: it is what stops the coolest smoke falling
// forty stops below the core.
//
// Fetch the source first: scenes/vdb/fetch.sh (explosion is CC-BY).
(
    version: 2,
    ops: [
        Settings((name: "main", resolution: Some((960, 540)), max_bounces: Some(32))),
        Camera((
            name: "main",
            position: Some((14.0, 100.0, 340.0)),
            look_at: Some((14.0, 100.0, 5.0)),
            vfov_degrees: Some(48.0),
        )),
        Environment((name: "sky", tint: Some((0.02, 0.03, 0.05)))),

        Mesh((name: "shell", source: Some(MediumBounds))),
        Material((name: "inert")),
        Medium((
            name: "fire",
            absorption: Some((0.01, 0.01, 0.01)),
            scattering: Some((0.06, 0.06, 0.06)),
            anisotropy: Some(0.2),
            volume: Some(Some((
                path: "sources/explosion.vdb",
                temperature_grid: Some("temperature"),
                temperature_scale: 4000.0,
                temperature_offset: 1200.0,
                emission: (400.0, 400.0, 400.0),
            ))),
        )),
        Instance((
            name: "fire",
            mesh: Some("shell"),
            material: Some("inert"),
            medium: Some(Some("fire")),
        )),
    ],
)
